{"kind":"assert","text":"Review for Hugh: check recovery scope against the original conditions.\n\nThe resident-writer history exposes a gap that a successor link alone cannot prevent. Original #9695/#10348 covered authority-command guards, GitHub observation routing and a shared resolver. Retirement #11998 preserved the remaining scope in an assert. Recovery #13162/#13316 then delivered the authority-command guards correctly. The connector and shared resolver were absent from that recovery's conditions and remained unassigned.\n\n| Original outcome | Current evidence | Disposition |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Four authority-command guards | Approved 148c5c0e, sealed receipt 6821a1c8 | Delivered; keep closed |\n| Connector routing through the advertised resident, including the local override | Current [connector](cmd/gitseq-github/main.go@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:503) ignores the advertisement; the isolated signed-submission probe appends locally with zero resident calls and rejects `--server -` | Recovered in [#20112](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3Ada2018c951453e4cfb6b6ac6485bd96a6e43ef9e) |\n| One resolver shared by gs and the connector | The [routing decision](cmd/gs/main.go@1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8:2299) remains private to gs | Also in #20112 |\n\nThe [history and source evidence](recovery-scope-evidence.json) includes the explicit residual and the narrower recovery conditions. The [four-case probe](routing-probe.json) uses disposable workrooms and the real connector submit function; it does not claim a live GitHub end-to-end run. The authority recovery's approval was sound for its stated scope.\n\nRecommendation for [#20013](http://127.0.0.1:7777/#/thread/git%3Asha1%3A5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8%23git%3Asha1%3Aa18edda93c0c33185ae944093fbc7b997b583568): whenever a recovery splits or restates an older request, give each original outcome a short disposition in the existing request or retirement text: delivered with evidence, still assigned with a live request, or deliberately abandoned by the responsible actor with a reason. A completed narrower successor accounts for its own conditions only. Keep the structural successor check, and make clear that it cannot establish semantic coverage on its own.\n\nUse a small table only where the scope actually splits; unchanged full-scope replacements need one sentence. This is review input for the existing safeguards design, using its existing records and lifecycle states. #20112 already assigns the implementation gap. No new policy is adopted here.","body":{"head":"1fba3d550091f720e48521bb89f222bd4c218af8","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:10017b454f7f8083bb050934339ef1192ea1dfa2, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:40943e9109500141671809df6f4adc2aa10e8102, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4eb6ed282bdb85fdccf2f0a6e989f8105fcf600c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:66e0e12172925f497f0dde1b910e705b157c08e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:da2018c951453e4cfb6b6ac6485bd96a6e43ef9e stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:02ce62ac39d438188a2ab6ac783b4edf22d7bd5e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:06022b8f3b6c8427f472855156801c4ecbcc532c and 119 more"}}